--- text
[PRODUCT_NAME] is working normally again

The service is working normally again. The problem started at
[EVENT_TIME], ended at [RESOLVED_TIME], and affected
[AFFECTED_SCOPE]. Both times carry their timezone. The details are
below, and you do not need the first email to follow them.

Incident summary

Status: [INCIDENT_STATUS]
Started: [EVENT_TIME]
Resolved: [RESOLVED_TIME]
Duration: [INCIDENT_DURATION]
Affected: [AFFECTED_SCOPE]

Here is what went wrong, in plain terms. [INCIDENT_CAUSE] The fault
is corrected, and we are changing how that part of the system works.

You do not need to do anything. If a page failed to load or a
request did not go through while the incident was running, try it
once more now. You do not need to sign in again or change your
password.

A fuller write-up, with the full timeline and the changes we are
making, will be published on the status page:

[STATUS_PAGE_URL]

We are sorry this happened. The failure was ours.

If something on your account still looks wrong, reply to this email
or write to [SUPPORT_EMAIL]. A real person reads every message.

[SIGNOFF_NAME], [COMPANY_NAME]
